title: War of the Powers

@certification
# prose-audit: Grade A — The oath crisis is framed from Lewica's role, with institutional pressure hidden behind concrete legal and civic choices.
title: War of the Powers I — the oath
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.trz_certification_event_done = 1;
Q.pres_2020_phase = "Certification contested";
Q.trz_inauguration_status = "President-elect — oath contested";
const margin = Number(Q.pres_runoff_margin) || 0;
const restraint = Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) || 50;
const courtTrust = Number(Q.judicial_legitimacy) || 36;
const pisCapacity = Number(Q.pis_org_resources) || 9;
Q.trz_obstruction_pressure = Math.max(
    20,
    Math.min(
        88,
        Math.round(
            58 - margin * 2.4 +
            Math.max(0, 50 - restraint) * 0.45 +
            Math.max(0, 42 - courtTrust) * 0.30 +
            pisCapacity * 0.65
        )
    )
);
Q.trz_cohabitation_temperature = 24;
Q.news_headline =
    "PiS contests the road from Trzaskowski's victory to the presidential oath";
!}

= August 2020 — The office is not yet his

PiS accepts that votes were counted and attacks every institution that must
turn the result into power. Loyal lawyers challenge the ballot, Sejm Marshal
**Elżbieta Witek** delays the National Assembly and government media calls the
result foreign and urban. We must make the oath unavoidable without teaching
voters that presidents take office through our pressure alone.

[? if trz_obstruction_pressure >= 65: The legal challenges, hostile media and
Marshal's delay now reinforce one another; a routine transition is no longer
available.?][? if trz_obstruction_pressure < 65: PiS can obstruct the ceremony,
but the certified count and functioning institutions still give us room to
hold the line.?]

- @certification_legal
- @certification_public
- @certification_bargain

