    "Witek blocks the oath and claims temporary presidential powers";
!}

Witek lets Duda's term expire without convening the oath and invokes the
"other reasons for not assuming office" clause to claim temporary presidential
duties. That reading is disputed precisely because her own delay created the
obstacle. Article 129 still leaves election validity to the Supreme Court; the
Marshal cannot order a new ballot herself.

Allies keep Poland inside its treaties but postpone senior meetings and ask
which signatures Warsaw can honour. The acting claim has succeeded for now.
It cannot become Witek's presidential term, and it cannot create a rerun
without a court judgment.

- @certification_continue: Continue to the next August file

