= October 2020 — The judgment reaches the wards

Julia Przyłębska, president of the disputed Constitutional Tribunal, announces
that terminating a pregnancy because of severe fetal impairment is
unconstitutional. Hospitals begin calling patients before the judgment is
even published; doctors ask which treatment may now expose them to a
prosecutor.

Marta Lempart, co-founder of the All-Poland Women's Strike, is calling people
into the streets. Lewica MP and feminist organiser Katarzyna Kotula wants the
party beside them without turning their anger into another opposition logo.
Across the chamber, PiS leader Jarosław Kaczyński presents the judgment as
settled law.

President Rafał Trzaskowski cannot veto a court judgment or restore access by
decree. He can challenge the panel's legitimacy, submit later legislation and
say now what he would sign. Our choice is whether that promise belongs to a
parliamentary front, an independent movement or a return to compromise.

- @tribunal_palace_bill
- @tribunal_movement
- @tribunal_compromise

@tribunal_palace_bill
title: Put one restoration bill between the Palace and the street
subtitle: Tie Lewica and KO to a promised signature; PiS and Konfederacja can campaign against one opposition front.
on-arrival: abortion_strategy = "Palace restoration front"; trz_abortion_signature = 1; trz_abortion_veto_policy = "Will sign statutory abortion restoration"; president_relation += 8; ko_relation += 5; p2050_relation += 2; feminist_trust += 8; judicial_legitimacy += 5; trz_right_fragmentation += 7; trz_right_backlash += 10; far_right_agenda += 5; pis_poll_momentum += 0.2; konf_poll_momentum += 0.4; rival_relation_pis_ko -= 5; news_headline = "The Palace promises a signature on abortion-law restoration"

Kotula and the opposition lawyers leave the Palace with a draft and an
unambiguous promise: if Parliament restores legal abortion, Trzaskowski will
sign. Women calling hospitals still have no new law tonight, but they can see
the route we are asking them to fight for.

Kaczyński and Konfederacja answer by folding the Palace, Lewica and the marches
into one enemy. We gain a constitutional ally and accept that the movement's
demand will now be judged against his timetable as well as ours.

- @poland_hub: Carry the restoration fight back to the leadership table

@tribunal_movement
title: Give the Women's Strike means without claiming its mandate
subtitle: Fund lawyers, rooms and organisers under Lempart's control; give up the certainty of a presidential signature.
on-arrival: abortion_strategy = "Autonomous movement support"; trz_abortion_signature = 0; trz_abortion_veto_policy = "No advance commitment"; feminist_trust += 12; movement_autonomy += 10; organiser_energy += 7; progressive_credibility += 5; president_relation -= 4; barons_dissent += 4; trz_right_backlash += 5; news_headline = "The Women's Strike refuses to become the President's movement"

Our district offices become legal clinics, printing rooms and places to sleep;
the lightning bolt remains on the leaflets and the party rose does not. Lempart
and the local organisers decide where the crowds go and who speaks for them.

Trzaskowski receives no request for an advance promise. Feminist organisers
trust us more for resisting capture, while party veterans complain that we
have financed a force we cannot direct. The street keeps its own voice and
loses the simplest guarantee at the end of the parliamentary road.

- @poland_hub: Carry the movement decision back to the leadership table

@tribunal_compromise
title: Ask the President to restore the old compromise
subtitle: Win a plausible route through PSL by stopping short of legal abortion; the march will hear retreat, not restoration.
on-arrival: abortion_strategy = "Presidential compromise"; trz_abortion_signature = 1; trz_abortion_veto_policy = "Will sign restoration of the 1993 compromise"; president_relation += 5; psl_relation += 6; barons_dissent -= 4; feminist_trust -= 10; progressives_dissent += 8; trz_right_fragmentation += 4; trz_right_backlash += 3; news_headline = "The Palace offers its signature to restore the old compromise"

Trzaskowski promises to sign a return to the pre-judgment settlement.
Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz, leader of PSL, says his deputies can discuss that
line; hospitals would at least recover the fetal-impairment ground the Tribunal
has removed.

Lempart and Kotula refuse to call the 1993 restrictions a victory. The wider
vote hunt becomes easier, but part of the Women's Strike now turns its anger
toward a Left that answered a constitutional retreat with another compromise.

- @poland_hub: Carry the compromise back to the leadership table

@judicial_war
# prose-audit: Grade A — Ziobro, Bodnar, opposition leaders and affected judges make the institutional stakes legible; each exit preserves the limits of veto, European process or cabinet delivery.
title: War of the Powers III — veto government
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: trz_judicial_war_done = 1; trz_cohabitation_temperature += 10; institutional_issue_salience += 12; news_headline = "PiS sends its judicial offensive to a hostile President"

= February 2021 — Two centres of legality

Justice Minister Zbigniew Ziobro sends the Palace another package of court
appointments and disciplinary rules. Prime Minister Mateusz Morawiecki calls
it administration; President Rafał Trzaskowski calls it an attempt to make the
government its own judge. Public television supplies the simpler phrase:
**veto government**.

Adam Bodnar, the Commissioner for Human Rights, brings cases from judges facing
disciplinary proceedings and citizens whose hearings disappear into the
backlog. KO leader Borys Budka and Polska 2050 founder Szymon Hołownia want one
democratic line. Our MPs must decide whether that line is an absolute veto,
European litigation or a bargain for pandemic relief.

The constitutional limit matters. Trzaskowski can stop a statute; he cannot
reinstate a removed judge, command a hospital or make Luxembourg hear a case
by presidential order.

- @judicial_veto_front
- @judicial_europe
- @judicial_trade

@judicial_veto_front
title: Unite every democratic party behind one veto list
subtitle: Budka and Hołownia help make two vetoes legible; TVP can blame one President for stopping the state.
on-arrival: trz_palace_strategy = "Common veto front"; trz_vetoes += 2; president_relation += 8; ko_relation += 6; p2050_relation += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 8; constitutional_restraint += 6; trz_right_fragmentation += 8; trz_right_backlash += 9; far_right_agenda += 4; pis_poll_momentum += 0.25; konf_poll_momentum += 0.3; rival_relation_pis_ko -= 6; news_headline = "Two presidential vetoes stop the judicial package"

Budka, Hołownia and our parliamentary club publish the same list of red lines.
Trzaskowski vetoes the appointments statute and the disciplinary bill; Bodnar
and the judges no longer have to guess which opposition party will trade them
away.

Nothing damaged is repaired, and the files can return under another title.
Morawiecki loses two laws but gains months of broadcasts in which one man at
the Palace prevents an elected majority from governing.

- @poland_hub: Return to the February leadership table

@judicial_europe
title: Build the cases that can reach Luxembourg
subtitle: Give disciplined judges a European forum; Ziobro and Konfederacja turn Brussels into the defendant.
on-arrival: trz_palace_strategy = "European judicial escalation"; president_relation += 5; ko_relation += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 10; constitutional_restraint += 3; trz_right_fragmentation += 6; trz_right_backlash += 12; far_right_agenda += 6; konf_poll_momentum += 0.5; minority_safety -= 1; news_headline = "The Palace internationalises the judicial conflict"

Bodnar's office, judicial associations and Lewica lawyers build the cases from
which domestic judges can refer questions to the Court of Justice. Our MEPs
take the same evidence to Věra Jourová, the European Commission vice-president
responsible for values and transparency. The Palace supplies political cover,
not a fictitious presidential appeal.

Judges gain time and an outside forum. Ziobro gains a campaign in which Polish
law is supposedly written in Brussels, and Konfederacja carries that suspicion
from the courts to every minority organisation already accused of importing
foreign demands.

- @poland_hub: Return to the February leadership table

@judicial_trade
title: Let one appointments law pass for a pandemic bargain
subtitle: Put hospitals and households into the agreement; only Morawiecki's cabinet can deliver, and the common veto front will break.
on-arrival: trz_palace_strategy = "Selective cohabitation bargain"; trz_pandemic_bargain_pending = 1; household_policy_pressure += 5; health_policy_pressure += 4; pis_relation += 6; president_relation += 2; ko_relation -= 6; p2050_relation -= 3; judicial_legitimacy -= 5; constitutional_restraint -= 4; trz_right_fragmentation += 10; trz_right_backlash += 2; last_policy_stage = "Negotiated concession"; last_policy_authority = "President and PiS cabinet"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "A Palace–government bargain splits the judicial package"

The Palace withholds a veto from one appointments law. In return, Morawiecki
puts household protection and hospital capacity into a written April package.
Nurses, patients and families receive dates and promises, not yet staff or
money; implementation still belongs to his Council of Ministers.

Budka and Hołownia call the exception the end of a common constitutional
front. We can answer that legality must also keep people alive. Until the
cabinet delivers, both accusations remain true.

- @poland_hub: Return to the February leadership table

@palace_offensive
# prose-audit: Grade A — Biedroń, Bodnar and Dziemianowicz-Bąk embody three positive uses of the presidency, with every result distinguishing a pledge or proposal from passage and delivery.
title: War of the Powers IV — what the pen is for
