= April 2021 — A presidency needs a positive verb

Vetoes have made Rafał Trzaskowski the government's most visible opponent.
They have not opened a clinic, protected a tenant or counted a single vote in
the Sejm. He can introduce legislation and promise what he will sign; Mateusz
Morawiecki still commands the ministries and Jarosław Kaczyński still counts
the governing majority.

[? if trz_pandemic_bargain_implemented: The February bargain has now produced
household protection and hospital capacity through Morawiecki's Council of
Ministers. Nurses and families see real relief, while government television
gives PiS the credit and describes the Palace as a supplicant.?][? if not
trz_pandemic_bargain_implemented: There is no cross-party delivery to exhibit.
Every positive promise must still survive a hostile cabinet and 231 votes.?]

Robert Biedroń, Wiosna leader and Lewica's former presidential candidate,
arrives with equality organisations asking for two written no-veto pledges.
Commissioner Adam Bodnar wants the Palace to remain a shield for courts, public
media and elections. Lewica MP Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk brings mayors,
nurses and tenants who want the prestige of the office turned toward everyday
government. We can lend Trzaskowski only one definition of his presidency.

- @palace_rights
- @palace_institutions
- @palace_social

@palace_rights
title: Give Biedroń two promises in writing
subtitle: Abortion restoration and marriage equality receive no-veto pledges; PSL retreats and the right finds one culture-war target.
on-arrival: trz_palace_strategy = "Equality compact"; trz_abortion_signature = 1; trz_marriage_signature = 1; trz_abortion_veto_policy = "Will sign legal abortion restoration"; trz_marriage_veto_policy = "Will sign marriage equality"; president_relation += 10; ko_relation += 5; progressive_credibility += 9; feminist_trust += 8; psl_relation -= 8; trz_right_fragmentation += 9; trz_right_backlash += 15; far_right_agenda += 8; pis_poll_momentum += 0.35; konf_poll_momentum += 0.7; rival_relation_pis_ko -= 6; rival_relation_ko_psl -= 4; news_headline = "Trzaskowski promises not to veto abortion reform or marriage equality"

Biedroń and the equality organisations leave with the President's name beneath
two sentences: he will sign abortion restoration and marriage equality. Women
denied care and couples denied recognition finally know that the last desk in
the process will not stop them.

No law has passed and no majority has been found. PSL leader Władysław
Kosiniak-Kamysz backs away from the compact; PiS and Konfederacja discover that
two rights can be made into one culture-war campaign. We have made the Palace
pen useful and made winning the Sejm indispensable.

- @poland_hub: Return to the April leadership table

@palace_institutions
title: Keep Bodnar's democratic shield intact
subtitle: Courts, public media and clean elections hold the broad opposition together; equality groups leave without a promise.
on-arrival: trz_palace_strategy = "Institutional presidency"; trz_marriage_signature = 0; trz_marriage_veto_policy = "No advance commitment"; president_relation += 6; ko_relation += 5; psl_relation += 4; p2050_relation += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 6; constitutional_restraint += 6; trz_right_fragmentation += 5; trz_right_backlash += 4; news_headline = "The Palace keeps its offensive on institutions"

Bodnar's cases become the centre of a presidential programme: repair the
courts, protect independent media and make the next count harder to dispute.
KO, PSL and Polska 2050 can all stand beneath it, and the Palace remains a
place where institutional damage is named rather than normalised.

Biedroń leaves without a promise on marriage equality. The broad front is
real because the disputed rights have been left outside it; women and LGBT+
families learn that a presidency can defend the rules without saying what the
rules should deliver for them.

- @poland_hub: Return to the April leadership table

@palace_social
title: Put Dziemianowicz-Bąk's social programme beside one rights pledge
subtitle: Promise an abortion signature and sponsor health, housing and local government; ministers keep the budgets and mayors inherit the expectations.
on-arrival: trz_palace_strategy = "Social cohabitation"; trz_abortion_signature = 1; trz_marriage_signature = 0; trz_abortion_veto_policy = "Will sign abortion restoration"; trz_marriage_veto_policy = "No advance commitment"; president_relation += 7; household_policy_pressure += 4; health_policy_pressure += 3; local_network += 3; labor_credibility += 4; ko_relation += 2; trz_right_fragmentation += 7; trz_right_backlash += 7; pis_poll_momentum += 0.15; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "President as bill sponsor and prospective signatory"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The Palace combines a rights pledge with a social programme"

Trzaskowski promises to sign abortion restoration and introduces a programme
for hospital staffing, housing and local-government finance. Nurses, tenants
and mayors acquire a national sponsor; they do not acquire a budget, because
Morawiecki's ministers still control every service named from the Palace.

Marriage equality is left outside the pledge. We gain a presidency that speaks
our social language and the responsibility for explaining every month in which
its proposals remain paper.

- @poland_hub: Return to the April leadership table

@rights_vote
# prose-audit: Grade A — The rights test distinguishes a presidential pledge from a Sejm majority and narrates both passage and defeat from Lewica's view.
title: War of the Powers V — test the majority
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: trz_rights_vote_done = 1; opposition_reset_event_done = 1; news_headline = "The opposition decides which presidential promise to test in the Sejm"

= June 2021 — A bill for the President's desk

The United Right is divided but still governs. We can organise only one
confrontation before the merger congress, and a promised presidential signature
is not the parliamentary majority needed to reach his desk.

- @rights_vote_abortion
- @rights_vote_marriage
- @rights_vote_institutions

@rights_vote_abortion
title: Put statutory abortion restoration to a vote
subtitle: Available only if Trzaskowski has promised not to veto it.
choose-if: trz_abortion_signature = 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Palace has made no reliable signature commitment.
on-arrival: {!
Q.trz_rights_bill = "Abortion-law restoration";
Q.trz_rights_bill_votes = Math.max(
    180,
    Math.min(
        250,
        Math.round(
            186 +
            (Number(Q.trz_right_fragmentation) || 0) * 1.08 +
            Math.max(
                0,
                (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 16) - 16
            ) * 0.55 +
            Math.max(0, (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 24) - 24) * 0.22 +
            Math.max(0, (Number(Q.ko_relation) || 44) - 44) * 0.16
        )
    )
);
if (Q.trz_rights_bill_votes >= 231) {
    Q.trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Passed and signed";
    Q.abortion_law_enacted = 1;
    Q.abortion_reform_stage = Math.max(
        Number(Q.abortion_reform_stage) || 0,
        3
    );
    Q.abortion_reform_defined = 1;
    Q.abortion_reform_settled = 1;
    Q.abortion_reform_proposal_stage = Q.abortion_reform_stage;
    Q.abortion_reform_next_stage = Q.abortion_reform_stage;
    Q.abortion_reform_progress = Math.max(
        Number(Q.abortion_reform_progress) || 0,
        60
    );
    Q.abortion_rewrite_pending = 0;
    Q.abortion_cabinet_deadline = 0;
    Q.feminist_trust += 14;
    Q.progressive_credibility += 10;
    Q.judicial_legitimacy += 6;
    Q.president_relation += 8;
    Q.trz_right_backlash += 16;
    Q.far_right_agenda += 8;
    Q.pis_poll_momentum += 0.45;
    Q.konf_poll_momentum += 0.75;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Trzaskowski signs the abortion-restoration law";
} else {
    Q.trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Defeated in the Sejm";
    Q.public_trust -= 2;
    Q.feminist_trust += 3;
    Q.trz_right_backlash += 7;
    Q.konf_poll_momentum += 0.3;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The abortion-restoration bill falls before reaching the President";
}
!}
go-to: rights_result

@rights_vote_marriage
title: Put marriage equality to a vote
subtitle: Available only with an explicit presidential no-veto pledge.
choose-if: trz_marriage_signature = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Trzaskowski has not promised to sign marriage equality.
on-arrival: {!
Q.trz_rights_bill = "Marriage equality";
Q.trz_rights_bill_votes = Math.max(
    170,
    Math.min(
        246,
        Math.round(
            180 +
            (Number(Q.trz_right_fragmentation) || 0) * 1.16 +
            Math.max(
                0,
                (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 16) - 16
            ) * 0.60 +
            Math.max(0, (Number(Q.ko_relation) || 44) - 44) * 0.20 +
            Math.max(0, (Number(Q.psl_relation) || 24) - 24) * 0.12
        )
    )
);
if (Q.trz_rights_bill_votes >= 231) {
    Q.trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Passed and signed";
    Q.progressive_credibility += 14;
    Q.minority_safety += 12;
    Q.president_relation += 9;
    Q.trz_right_backlash += 20;
    Q.far_right_agenda += 10;
    Q.pis_poll_momentum += 0.5;
    Q.konf_poll_momentum += 0.9;
    Q.news_headline = "Trzaskowski signs marriage equality into law";
} else {
    Q.trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Defeated in the Sejm";
    Q.public_trust -= 3;
    Q.progressive_credibility += 3;
    Q.trz_right_backlash += 10;
    Q.konf_poll_momentum += 0.45;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Marriage equality falls before reaching the President";
}
!}
go-to: rights_result

@rights_vote_institutions
title: Send another judicial-repair law instead
subtitle: A broader coalition and a safer presidential signature.
on-arrival: {!
Q.trz_rights_bill = "Judicial repair";
const democraticRepairVotes =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.other_seats) || 0);
const repairDefectors = Math.round(
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.trz_right_fragmentation) || 0) * 0.45 +
    Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 16) - 16
    ) * 0.30
);
Q.trz_rights_bill_votes = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460,
        Math.round(democraticRepairVotes + repairDefectors)
    )
);
if (Q.trz_rights_bill_votes >= 231) {
    Q.trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Passed and signed";
    Q.judicial_legitimacy += 10;
    Q.constitutional_restraint += 7;
    Q.president_relation += 5;
    Q.ko_relation += 4;
    Q.psl_relation += 3;
    Q.p2050_relation += 3;
    Q.progressive_credibility -= 2;
    Q.trz_right_backlash += 5;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Trzaskowski signs a narrow judicial-repair law";
} else {
    Q.trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Defeated in the Sejm";
    Q.judicial_repair_mandate += 3;
    Q.public_trust -= 1;
    Q.trz_right_backlash += 2;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The judicial-repair bill falls before reaching the President";
}
!}
go-to: rights_result

@rights_result
title: The signature test
new-page: true

**[+ trz_rights_bill +]** receives **[+ trz_rights_bill_votes +] votes**.
Outcome: **[+ trz_rights_bill_outcome +]**.

[? if trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Passed and signed": The promised signature is
immediate. We have made the cohabitation presidency a route to law as well as a
veto point; the right begins the next campaign around reversing the result. ?]

[? if trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Defeated in the Sejm": Trzaskowski never gets
the choice to sign or veto. Our pledge remains real, but the governing majority
in the Sejm matters more than the occupant of the Palace. ?]

- @poland_hub: Continue to the merger congress
